The 22 SVGs are derived from icons/<same filename>.svg at that revision.
The palette is based on styles/ui-variables.less and the associations on
styles/components/icons/mapping.less. Seti is the source of VS Code's built-in
Seti file-icon theme; see microsoft/vscode/extensions/theme-seti/build/
update-icon-theme.js. No VS Code font files are included.

Adaptations:
- All view boxes are normalized to "4 4 24 24" for the existing 16px icon slot.
- default.svg and zip.svg use translate(-3.2 0) scale(.032) to normalize their
  original 1200x1000 coordinates; vue.svg uses translate(-2 1) scale(.03).
- docker.svg is inset by translate(1.6 1.6) scale(.9) to avoid edge clipping.
- Embedded fills match the dark palette. GPUI's Svg element renders an alpha
  mask, so file_panel.rs explicitly supplies the per-type color from
  src/components/file_panel/file_icons.rs; SVG fills alone are insufficient.
- zip.svg's white zipper details become transparent cutouts via a luminance
  mask so the zipper survives GPUI's alpha-mask rendering in either theme.
- Rust is orange, configuration files purple, and Git files red, intentionally
  replacing Seti's gray variants for those frequently encountered file types.
- Colored glyphs use VS Code Seti's 90%-per-channel adjustment in light mode.
  Unknown files instead use a legible neutral gray on light backgrounds.
- The resolver is a curated, case-insensitive set of common extensions and
  filenames, not a full port of VS Code's language registry or every icon theme.
  Unknown formats have a generic fallback. Related formats may share a glyph.

These are bundled local assets; there are no runtime network requests or new
package dependencies. Preserve this notice and LICENSE when updating assets.
